Title: GREYHARBOR
Episode: 105 "The Third Tide"
Credit: Original fixture material written for the Canon AI test harness.

EXT. GREYHARBOR DOCKS - DAWN

Cole's body bag leaves on the coroner's boat. Nobody waves.

Mara stands apart, coat buttoned over bruises. Lila approaches with a paper cup of coffee.

LILA
State police are asking who hated him.

MARA
That line reaches the causeway.

LILA
They are also asking who loved him.

Mara looks at the empty deputy's slip.

MARA
Shorter line.

INT. EDDA'S SHACK - DAY

The stove burns low. Edda reads copied ledger pages while Mara pins boat names to the wall.

EDDA
Four Thursday runs, same tide, same weight.

MARA
And no boat with that registry.

EDDA
Then it wasn't a boat. It was a promise wearing a boat's name.

INT. HARBORMASTER'S OFFICE - DAY

The office has been stripped of Tobias's things. The tide chart remains.

Tobias stands at the desk, dry-eyed and solid, tapping the chart with one finger.

TOBIAS
You're still counting boats, Mara. Count the people who need them gone.

MARA
I buried you.

TOBIAS
You buried the easy part.

EXT. FERRY SLIP - DAY

Gideon opens the Blue Gull's hold. Danny climbs down with a flashlight and a coil of rope.

GIDEON
Hatch stays chained until the third tide turns. If anybody boards, you keep breathing quiet.

DANNY
I'm tired of hiding in boxes.

GIDEON
Then pick a town with fewer boxes.

Gideon chains the hatch from outside.

INT. COURTHOUSE ARCHIVE - NIGHT

Mara unrolls a county map across a dusty table. Lila holds a lantern near the coastline.

Danny stands beside Mara at the courthouse map table, saltwater dripping from his cuffs.

DANNY
Black Osprey was a land parcel before it was a boat.

MARA
Who owns it?

LILA
Nobody, if the county book is telling the truth.

MARA
It never does.

INT. LILA'S APARTMENT - LATE NIGHT

Lila places a recorder on the table. Mara and Edda lean close.

ON THE RECORDER, COLE'S VOICE rasps through static.

COLE (V.O.)
Tobias kept a second list. If Mara finds it, burn the channel behind her.

Lila stops the tape.

LILA
He said it two nights before he died.

MARA
Then he was afraid before we knew enough to scare him.

EXT. OLD CHAPEL ROAD - NIGHT

Mara walks the road where the chapel used to pull the dark around itself. There are only black stones and weeds.

She finds a blue fishhook hanging from a bramble.

MARA
Danny?

No answer. The hook turns in the wind.

INT. FERRY HOLD - NIGHT

Danny sits in the chained hold, very much inside it, listening to footsteps cross the deck above.

The footsteps stop.

VOICE ABOVE
Blue hook means breathing.

Danny kills his flashlight.

FADE OUT.
